            ("What mouse and keyboard communication parameter measures how many times per second the device reports its position data to the USB bus?", "USB Polling Rate (measured in Hertz, e.g., 1,000 Hz = 1 ms)", ["DPI", "CPI", "Baud Rate"], "Standard USB polls at 125 Hz (8 ms delay); competitive gaming peripherals poll at 1,000 Hz (1 ms), 4,000 Hz, or 8,000 Hz (0.125 ms) to minimize input lag."),
            ("What short-range wireless personal area network standard operates in the 2.4 GHz ISM band, connecting mice, keyboards, and wireless headphones?", "Bluetooth (IEEE 802.15.1)", ["Wi-Fi (802.11)", "Zigbee", "NFC"], "Bluetooth uses frequency-hopping spread spectrum (FHSS) across 79 channels to resist interference, offering low power consumption (BLE)."),
            ("What low-latency proprietary wireless transmission technology uses dedicated 2.4 GHz USB dongles to match wired gaming mouse performance?", "2.4 GHz Wireless RF (e.g., Logitech Lightspeed, Razer HyperSpeed)", ["Standard Bluetooth", "Infrared", "Zigbee"], "Proprietary 2.4 GHz protocols achieve sub-1 millisecond transmission latency by bypassing standard Bluetooth protocol stack overhead."),
            ("What flat-panel display technology utilizes individual self-emissive organic pixels that turn off completely to achieve infinite contrast and true black?", "OLED (Organic Light-Emitting Diode)", ["IPS LCD", "VA LCD", "TN LCD"], "Because OLED requires no backlight, individual off pixels emit zero light, delivering perfect black levels and sub-millisecond response times."),
